<h2>When to wear a balaclava</h2>
<p>On cold, windy days and long chairlift rides, a balaclava covers the gaps between your helmet, goggles, and jacket collar, including the back of your neck and your ears. Thin balaclavas fit comfortably under a ski helmet without changing the helmet's fit much; thicker ones may need a helmet with a little extra room.</p>

<h2>When a neck gaiter is enough</h2>
<p>On milder days, a gaiter is easier to manage. You can pull it up over your nose on the lift and push it down when you get warm. It doesn't cover your head, so pair it with a helmet liner or rely on your helmet for warmth.</p>

<h2>Materials and fit</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Merino wool:</strong> warm, breathable, and resists odor.</li>
  <li><strong>Synthetic fleece or stretch fabrics:</strong> durable, quick-drying, often warmer per weight.</li>
  <li><strong>Windproof panels:</strong> some balaclavas add wind-blocking fabric over the face for very cold conditions.</li>
  <li><strong>Breathing and fog:</strong> look for a breathable or mesh mouth area, and keep the fabric below your goggles so warm breath doesn't fog the lens.</li>
  <li><strong>Thin profile under helmets:</strong> your helmet should still fit snugly with the balaclava on.</li>
</ul>
<p>Browse <%= gear_link "ski balaclavas", "balaclava" %> or <%= gear_link "neck gaiters", "neck gaiter" %>.</p>

<h2>Which should you get?</h2>
<p>If you ski cold places or run cold, get a thin balaclava for under your helmet. If you mostly ski milder days or spring, a gaiter covers you. Many skiers keep both and choose based on the forecast. For the rest of your outfit, see <%= link_to "what to wear skiing", guide_path("what-to-wear-skiing") %>, and check the conditions with <%= link_to "where it's snowing this week", where_is_it_snowing_path %>.</p>
<% faqs << { question: "Is a balaclava the same as a ski mask?", answer: "Usually. Most people use ski mask to mean a balaclava, a hood that covers the head, neck, and lower face. Ski mask can also mean a face-only cover." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "Can you wear a balaclava under a ski helmet?", answer: "Yes. Thin balaclavas are designed to fit under helmets. Your helmet should still fit snugly with it on." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "How do I stop my balaclava from fogging my goggles?", answer: "Keep the fabric below the goggle frame so your breath isn't directed into the lens, and choose a balaclava with a breathable or mesh mouth area." } %>
